[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115799,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Neuromas constitute a diverse group of peripheral nerve sheath tumours, some reactive and hyperplastic, that include traumatic neuroma (TN), solitary circumscribed neuroma (SCN), multiple endocrine neoplasia type&nbsp;2B (MEN2B)-associated mucosal neuroma, oral pseudoperineurioma (OPP), and <em>PIK3CA</em>-related overgrowth spectrum (PROS)-associated neuroma (<em>PIK3CA</em> neuroma).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115800,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9570/0 Solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115801,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F24 &amp; XH90Y8 Benign cutaneous neoplasms of neural or nerve sheath origin &amp; Solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n<p>8C12.5 Traumatic neuroma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>2F7A.0 MEN2B-mucosal neuroma</p>\r\n<p>8C4Y &amp; XH4UE6 Other specified disorders of nerve root, plexus, or peripheral nerves &amp; Neuroma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>LD2C &amp; XH4UE6 Overgrowth syndromes &amp; Neuroma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115802,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> for solitary circumscribed neuroma: palisaded encapsulated neuroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> for traumatic neuroma: amputation neuroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115803,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115804,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>TN occurs in areas of nerve injury including bones. SCN frequently affects facial skin and palate/gingiva. Most OPPs occur on the tongue. <em>PIK3CA</em> neuromas affect the tongue, lips, and cheek.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115805,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Neuromas manifest as single nodules (TN, SCN) or multiple nodules (<em>PIK3CA</em> neuroma, rarely in SCN) of &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm with the exception of TN. Many but not all TNs are painful; all other neuromas are asymptomatic. Multiple mucosal neuromas unrelated to MEN2B and PROS have been described {26708403}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115806,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>TN:</em> Middle-aged adults; more frequent in women.</p>\r\n<p><em>SCN:</em> Fifth to seventh decades of life; twice as common in men.</p>\r\n<p><em>OPP:</em> Young female patients.</p>\r\n<p><em>Mucosal neuromas:</em> Usually the first sign of MEN2B and of <em>PIK3CA</em>-related orofacial overgrowth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115807,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>TNs are the result of accidental or iatrogenic nerve injury or amputation. Although SCNs are considered hyperplastic lesions, trauma maybe a possible cause for oral SCN, whereas cutaneous lesions have been associated with acne. MEN2B- and <em>PIK3CA</em>-related neuromas are caused by germline <em>RET</em> and somatic <em>PIK3CA</em> mutations, respectively. Solitary OPPs are considered the result of trauma. Multiple OPPs can be encountered in PROS.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115808,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>TN:</em> Exuberant proliferation of disorganized peripheral nerve fascicles as part of nerve regeneration after nerve injury.</p>\r\n<p><em>SCN:</em> Intraneural fascicular Schwann cell proliferation.</p>\r\n<p><em>MEN2B and PIK3CA neuromas:</em> Enlargement of peripheral nerve bundles as part of <em>RET</em> germline mutations and <em>PIK3CA</em> somatic mutations, respectively.</p>\r\n<p><em>OPP:</em> Perineurial proliferation as part of apparent nerve injury or nerve enlargement as seen in PROS.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115809,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The size of TN varies. SCN and PROS-associated neuromas are small smooth nodules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115810,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>TN:</em> Disorganized Schwann cell fascicles surrounded by perineurium sprouting from severed nerve {30011306}.</p>\r\n<p><em>SCN:</em> Fungating, round, multinodular, or plexiform in the superficial dermis&nbsp;/ lamina propria, characterized by intersecting Schwann cell fascicles with nerve axons frequently revealing cracking artefact {20237984}.</p>\r\n<p><em>OPP:</em> Nerve fascicles showing complete or incomplete perineurium featuring thin, internally located, perineurial cell pseudo&ndash;onion bulbs {23645379}.</p>\r\n<p><em>PIK3CA neuroma:</em> Enlarged nerves with frequently hyperplastic perineurium or OPP. May share features with MEN2B necessitating clinicopathological correlation {28665924; 32770747}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115811,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not described</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115812,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>PIK3CA</em> variants in the majority of <em>PIK3CA</em> neuromas</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115813,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<p>TN: haphazardly arranged nerve fascicles.</p>\r\n<p>SCN: a fungating, multilobular/plexiform, circumscribed, partially encapsulated fascicular proliferation.</p>\r\n<p>OPP: pseudo&ndash;onion bulbs.</p>\r\n<p><em>PIK3CA</em> neuromas: enlarged nerves; thickened perineurium; OPP.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115814,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115815,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 340,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is excellent for all types described.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:13:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]